WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:16.660
Good morning, John. It's Monday, January 29th,
and I'm standing on top of Little Pisgah Mountain,

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:20.710
just like you were. Dad insisted that I use
this plane clip in the video. I don't know

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:21.830
why.

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:27.180
I actually filmed that video three days ago,
but you have no way of knowing that. How's

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:32.090
that for movie magic? So it's three days later
now, and we've done the jaunt to Athens, and

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:35.760
I'm at a friend's house. We've been having
a good time in Athens. It's a pretty nice

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.620
city; I suggest you try it on sometime.

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:43.160
Today's video is a short video because last
night, my friends and I spent quite a long

00:00:43.160 --> 00:00:50.820
time creating a project that I would like
to share with you, as it is inspired by you!

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:55.600
As an added bonus, you will get to see my
wife, Katherine. Apparently she’s not quite

00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:01.480
the yeti that your wife is, and will occasionally
come out in public. Also, you may notice featured

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:07.390
in this video, Brian Nuse and Jesslyn Shields,
two of my best friends, who live here in Athens

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:10.020
and assisted me with this project a very great
deal.

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:16.180
(Singing)
Will you miss me when I’m gone from your

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:24.189
pants?
Will you miss me when I'm gone from your pants?

00:01:24.189 --> 00:01:37.289
Will you miss me when I’m gone, gone, gone?
Will you miss me when I’m gone from your

00:01:37.289 --> 00:01:38.289
pants?

00:01:38.289 --> 00:01:45.340
(guitar and tambourine join in)
Will you miss me when I’m gone from your

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:52.270
pants?
Will you miss me when I’m gone? From your

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:57.070
pants!
Will you miss me when I’m gone, gone, gone?

00:01:57.070 --> 00:02:08.720
Will you miss me when I’m gone from your
pants?

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:09.890
(laughter)

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:15.580
That’s all! There you have it. I’ll see
you tomorrow.

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:19.300
You know how some DVDs have bonus features?
Well, Brotherhood 2.0 has bonus features too,

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:22.170
and you’re about to see one. You might expect
that “Will You Miss Me When I'm Gone from

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:25.740
Your Pants?” took more than one take to
film. It did. Here’s the first take.

00:02:25.740 --> 00:02:32.090
(singing)
Will you miss me when I’m gone from your

00:02:32.090 --> 00:02:35.420
pants?
Will… (Group bursts into laughter)

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:38.190
Katherine: That wasn’t even me!

